            <h2 class="section-title">Effective Date of Resignation</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <ul><li><strong>Rule:</strong> Date notice received OR date specified — whichever is LATER.</li><li><strong>Example 1:</strong> Received 15 Apr, specified 1 May → Effective 1 May (later).</li><li><strong>Example 2:</strong> Received 15 Apr, specified 1 Apr → Effective 15 Apr (can't be effective before receipt).</li><li><strong>Example 3:</strong> Received 15 Apr, no date → Effective 15 Apr.</li><li><strong>Why it matters:</strong> Determines (a) last date as director + liable for decisions, (b) 30-day clock for DIR-12/DIR-11, (c) last date as bank signatory.</li><li><strong>Patron advises:</strong> Optimal effective date strategy for Delhi directors.</li></ul>

            </div>
